                            cq:lastRolledoutBy="admin"
                            cq:panelTitle="Itinerary"
                            jcr:lastModified="{Date}2020-11-08T12:40:48.542-08:00"
                            jcr:lastModifiedBy="admin"
                            jcr:mixinTypes="[cq:LiveRelationship]"
                            jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                            sling:resourceType="weekender/components/contentfragment"
                            displayMode="singleText"
                            elementNames="itinerary"
                            fragmentPath="/content/dam/weekender-shared/en/adventures/napa-wine-tasting/napa-wine-tasting"
                            paragraphScope="all"
                            text="Napa Wine Tasting Morning: sparkling wine We leave the city at nine and start, as one should, with bubbles: a small producer on the cooler southern edge of the valley, with a walk through the vines and a look at the cellar. Midday: a hillside estate Up a winding road on the eastern side, a family has farmed the same slope for three generations. We taste their Cabernet from the barrel and from the bottle, and have a picnic lunch under the oaks with the valley below. Afternoon: the old vines The last visit is to a grower who works Zinfandel vines planted a century ago. A final tasting in the garden, and we are back in San Francisco by six."
                            variationName="master">
                            <par6
                                cq:lastRolledout="{Date}2020-11-08T12:40:48.566-08:00"
